tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Rights and Equal Treatment

In this alternate-history programme, we can seek protections against discrimination and arbitrary treatment based on sexuality or gender identity. Each proposal faces opposition within Parliament.

- @protection: Introduce protections against discrimination.
- @privacy: Limit arbitrary policing of private life and personal expression.
- @recognition: Establish a procedure for legal gender recognition.
- @return: Leave policy unchanged.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@protection
view-if: anti_discrimination = 0
on-arrival: anti_discrimination = 1; homosexual_rights += 1; AP_relation -= 5; TIP_relation += 4*(1-dissent); CGP_relation += 4*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition

Parliament adopts protections against discrimination. Implementation will require oversight of employers and public institutions.

@privacy
view-if: privacy_rights = 0
on-arrival: privacy_rights = 1; homosexual_rights += 1; AP_relation -= 5; TIP_relation += 4*(1-dissent); CGP_relation += 4*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition

The new rules limit arbitrary interference in private life and personal expression.

@recognition
view-if: trans_rights = 0
on-arrival: trans_rights = 1; homosexual_rights += 1; AP_relation -= 5; TIP_relation += 4*(1-dissent); CGP_relation += 4*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition

Parliament establishes a procedure for legal gender recognition, with safeguards for the people using it.
